<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  ETStage: 3 entry categorical colormap for HETstage (Evans and Hart
  (2003) extratropical transition stage, see D2D/README.md). Pair this
  with a styleRule range of -0.5 to 2.5 so each integer code below lands
  in the middle of one color bin instead of on a boundary between two:

    code 0  pre-onset            pale gray, half
                                  transparent     (0.85, 0.85, 0.85, 0.5)
    code 1  onset (B above 10 m) orange          (0.95, 0.60, 0.15, 1.0)
    code 2  complete (VTL < 0)   blue            (0.15, 0.35, 0.85, 1.0)

  Code 0 (pre-onset) is half transparent for the same reason
  CPS_CoreClass.cmap's neutral code is: a system that has not begun
  transition is not worth painting as an opaque fill over MSLP contours
  plotted underneath. The onset/complete colors reuse CPS_CoreClass's
  own shallow-warm-core orange and cold-core blue, since onset and
  completion are the same physical transition CPScat/HCPScat's
  shallow-warm-to-cold-core categories already track.

  File format: a root <colorMap> element containing an ordered list of
  <color r="" g="" b="" a=""/> entries, each component a float from 0.0
  to 1.0, in code order (this file's first <color> is code 0, and so
  on), same format and comment style as CPS_CoreClass.cmap; see that
  file's own comment for the VERIFY note on the element/attribute names
  against your site's actual .cmap schema.
-->
<colorMap>
        <color r="0.85" g="0.85" b="0.85" a="0.5"/>
        <color r="0.95" g="0.60" b="0.15" a="1.0"/>
        <color r="0.15" g="0.35" b="0.85" a="1.0"/>
</colorMap>
